{{Quote|Look around&mdash;your Mandalorians have been crushed. Only my droids remain now. Your battle is already lost.''"<br />"''We're not finished yet. My Gauntlet fighters have yet to enter the fight!|[[Grievous|General Grievous]] and Maul during a battle on [[Zanbar]]|<ref name="Son of Dathomir, Part One" />}}
The '''''Kom'rk''-class fighter/transport''', also known as '''''Kom'rk'' Class fighter transport''' or the '''Gauntlet starfighter''', was a type of [[starfighter]] and [[troop]] [[transport]] used by the [[Mandalorian]] splinter faction known as [[Death Watch]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. The fighters were utilized as part of a move by Death Watch leader [[Pre Vizsla]] to end [[Satine Kryze]]'s pacifist rule of [[Mandalore]] and restore the Mandalorians to their former warrior past. These ships were later used by [[Maul]]'s [[Shadow Collective]] army during [[Battle of Zanbar|battles on Zanbar]], [[Battle on Ord Mantell|Ord Mantell]], and [[Assault on Vizsla Keep 09|Vizsla Keep 09]]. During each of these battles, Maul utilized a gauntlet fighter called the [[Nightbrother (Gauntlet fighter)|''Nightbrother'']],<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|the-nightbrother|The Nightbrother}}</ref> colored red and black rather than the normal white and blue color scheme, as a transport and a Shadow Collective [[flagship]].<ref name="SoD">''[[Star Wars: Darth Maul — Son of Dathomir]]''</ref> During the reign of the [[Galactic Empire]], a gauntlet fighter known as the ''[[Splendour]]'' was owned by the [[Besalisk]] criminal [[Galus Vez]], who used it to race opponents on his private racing track, the [[Fool's Run]].<ref name="RR">{{RebelsMagCite|1|Ring Race}}</ref>

The [[Journeyman Protector|Mandalorian Protectors]] used a similar fighter known as the [[Fang-class Protectorate fighter|''Fang''-class Protectorate fighter ]].<ref name="Fang Fighter">{{Databank|fang-fighter|Fang Fighter}}</ref> During the time of the [[New Republic]], [[Bo-Katan Kryze]] utilized a [[Bo-Katan Kryze's Gauntlet starfighter|''Kom'rk''-class fighter]] in several occasions, including a [[Bombing of Kryze Castle|dogfight over Kalevala]].<ref name="Chapter 19" /> Thirty years after the [[Battle of Endor]],<ref name="Perfect Weapon Date">The [[Del Rey]] ''[[Star Wars]]'' timeline places "The Perfect Weapon" in between [[Canto Bight (novella collection)|''Canto Bight'']] and [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. {{SW|url=news/4-reasons-canto-bight-is-an-essential-read|text=4 Reasons ''Canto Bight'' Is an Essential Read}} states that ''Canto Bight'' takes place a few [[Standard day|days]] prior to [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']], which ''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' places in the same year as the ''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens''. ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates ''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'' to [[34 ABY]], meaning that both ''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'', ''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'', and ''Canto Bight'' take place in the same year. Because "The Perfect Weapon" takes place in between ''Canto Bight'' and ''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'', it must also take place in 34 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]].</ref> the retired pirate [[Delphi Kloda]] owned a Gauntlet called the ''[[Sparrowhawk]]'', which he lent to his former protege [[Bazine Netal]].<ref name="Perfect Weapon">"[[The Perfect Weapon]]"</ref>

==History==
===Clone Wars===
[[File:Drop-SeatBay-SWZ91.png|thumb|left|250px|Death Watch warriors deploy from a ''Kom'rk''-class fighter.]]
During the Clone Wars, the [[Death Watch]] used several of these fighters to evacuate their [[Deathwatch hideout|hideout]] at one of [[Concordia]]'s [[Concordian mines|mines]]. Death Watch then prepared several of these fighters to take part in taking [[Sundari]] when the Republic's Grand Army would arrive to occupy Mandalore.<ref name="DoM">{{TCW|Duchess of Mandalore}}</ref> However, when the Republic did not occupy Mandalore, Death Watch broke their ties with the Confederacy and took their fighters to their [[Carlac Death Watch camp|camp]] on [[Carlac]].<ref name="AFiN">{{TCW|A Friend in Need}}</ref>

Death Watch's commander [[Pre Vizsla]] and his second in command, [[Bo-Katan Kryze]] then took one of their fighters and found two [[Zabrak]]s; the renegade [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]] and his brother [[Savage Opress]]. Vizsla then took them to his [[Zanbar Death Watch camp|camp]] on [[Zanbar]]. Together, the Death Watch and the [[Sith]] agreed to form an [[Shadow Collective|alliance]] with Maul and other criminal syndicates. Maul, Vizsla and their forces then took their fighters to [[Black Sun]]'s [[Mustafar]] base, [[Gardulla Besadii the Elder|Gardulla the Hutt's]] [[Gardulla the Hutt's Palace|Palace]] on [[Nal Hutta]], and [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba the Hutt's]] [[Boba Fett's Palace|Palace]] on [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Eminence">{{TCW|Eminence (episode)}}</ref>

===Later history===
{{Quote|This is a Kom'rk Class fighter transport. I'll use this to drop you in and you will operate as a tight military unit.|Bo-Katan Kryze to the Children of the Watch|<ref name="Chapter 21">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 21: The Pirate}}</ref>}}
[[File:Gauntlet_on_Mandalore.png|thumb|left|250px|Bo-Katan's ship]]
[[Bo-Katan Kryze]] was in command of a [[Bo-Katan Kryze's Gauntlet starfighter|''Kom'rk''-class fighter]] on [[Lafete]]<ref name="Chapter 16">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 16: The Rescue}}</ref> around [[9 ABY]].<ref name="Mando Date">{{MandoDate|16}}</ref> She later used her starfighter to travel from [[Kalevala]] to [[Mandalore]] with [[R5-D4]] and [[Din Grogu|Grogu]].<ref name="Chapter 18">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 18: The Mines of Mandalore}}</ref> When she had returned to Kalevala, she was [[Bombing of Kryze Castle|attacked]] by [[TIE/IN interceptor]]s. She was able to destroy several interceptors, and utilized an [[heat-seeking missile]] to destroy a [[TIE/sa tactical bomber|TIE/sa bomber]], but eventually retreated after a backup of TIE interceptors arrived.<ref name="Chapter 19" /> Later, Kryze used her ship to drop two teams of [[Mandalorian warrior]]s to relieve [[Nevarro]] from a [[Pirate siege on Nevarro|pirate siege]] and to destroy [[Gorian Shard's pirate Corsair|Gorian Shard's Corsair]] with the help of [[Din Djarin]] and [[Din Djarin's N-1 starfighter|his]] [[N-1 starfighter]].<ref name="Chapter 21" />

In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="TROS Date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']] to one [[Standard year|year]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. As ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of ''The Force Awakens'' to [[34 ABY]], the events of ''The Rise of Skywalker'' must occur in [[35 ABY]].</ref> Gauntlet starfighters were part of a [[Citizens' Fleet|fleet]] assembled by [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] to assist the [[Resistance]] during the [[Battle of Exegol|battle]] against the [[Sith Eternal military|Sith Eternal forces]] over the [[planet]] [[Exegol]].<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

{{Ship-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Gauntlet starfighters were created for the [[canon]] animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''.

